WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.635
Let's finish by reviewing the main ideas from Module
5 When AND

00:00:05.661 --> 00:00:09.720
and OR appear together use parentheses to make the
intended grouping clear

00:00:10.637 --> 00:00:16.449
Remember that SQL uses three logical states TRUE
FALSE and UNKNOWN Treat

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:22.544
null values explicitly Use IS NULL Boolean
predicates and null-safe comparisons

00:00:22.557 --> 00:00:27.621
when the business rule requires them For text
normalize blank values before

00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:32.905
using fallbacks With case expressions remember that
the first true branch wins

00:00:33.085 --> 00:00:38.678
so branch order matters And finally test edge cases
Check null

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:44.425
values blanks zero exact thresholds and overlapping
conditions Throughout

00:00:44.451 --> 00:00:47.596
this module you were able to run SQL directly in the
browser

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.565
and you can also copy those same examples into
pgAdmin for additional

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:56.565
PostgreSQL practice The goal is not only to write
SQL that runs

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.920
The goal is to write SQL that accurately represents
the rule you

00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:01.513
intended
